Rationing against shadow prices at three depths of disruption. The capacity loss is 10, 30 and 50 per cent; each cell is twenty seeds. The two institutions are not ranked by any single metric: at the deepest shock rationing delivers more output and more welfare but records a higher shortage rate, and at the shallowest it delivers less output. Generated by `scripts/paper_tables.py` from `results/B4`. Source: `reference_results/` (the Lead's independent reference run, cross-checked against the experiment layer in `reference_results/CROSSCHECK.md`).
